      "summary": "Applications put their toolbar in their window's title bar: buttons, toggles, menus, tabs and a search field, described as a JSON document (`HEADER_SCHEMA`) and drawn by the desktop, so every bar follows the theme and the writing direction, works by keyboard and screen reader, and fits a narrow window by moving what does not fit into one \"More\" menu. A framed page calls `setHeader` and hears uses at `onHeader`; a shipped module has the same pair on its context. Every use, the person's and the assistant's, goes through the kernel's own `tangle_os_header` contract (`header.list`, `header.activate`) under grants and into the ledger; an item marked `assistant: false` is kept from the assistant. Calendar moves its month controls into its header bar and Settings its search.",
      "id": "header-bars"
    }
  ],
